# Volt kit door and fender fit — 3 November 2026

The owner rejected the previous body-kit pass: skirts covered the door bottoms and all four approaches to the wheel openings left exposed gaps. This correction lowers all fifteen skirts below the doors and fits both skirt ends and all four bumper returns to the actual painted fender curves. It supersedes the previous refinement's appearance acceptance; its passing coverage counters did not establish correct door/fender fit.

VDF01 keeps the whole skirt beneath the factory door-bottom datum of 0.31 in the reference model. Variant tops are now 0.281–0.298, replacing 0.355–0.455 including the former rear rise. VDF02 replaces fixed ±0.90 skirt ends and ±1.94 bumper ends with height-dependent points sampled from the existing fender openings. Each visible attachment is within 1.1 mm of that reference boundary, including the intentional 1 mm outward skin offset. These dimensions are in the existing unscaled model coordinates. VDF03 refreshes module/photo revision `volt-door-fender-fit-2` and the prepared representations. Original, item IDs, ownership, other kit categories and canonical handling remain.

