The old rectangular tire-bounds test reported 117 failures once the skirts and corners were correctly extended to the curved fenders. Bounds now remain the broad rejection step; overlapping bounds proceed to actual convex tire-hull versus kit-triangle collision queries. This removes rectangular empty-space false positives while retaining real clearance assertions. The positive obstruction check verifies that a disabled or empty physics world cannot silently pass the fixture.

The former construction test also demanded sill coverage at height 0.34, above the factory door bottoms. That incorrect coverage sample is replaced with 0.25/0.265/0.28 inside the corrected lower skirt; complete bumper and corner coverage, shell topology and geometry budgets remain. New independent door/fender tests reject the previously accepted parts rather than merely accepting the revised sampling window.

All engine launches use pinned Godot 4.7.2 through `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py`, isolated task APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA and empty BMT_API_URL. Reproduce with `python scripts/run_volt_fit.py <log-name> res://tests/<script>.gd <engine flags> -- <script flags>`. Each evidence log begins with its exact command and records exit status. The wrapper rejects other engine/script errors; Windows' existing certificate-store read error is retained. `run_volt_fit.py` now uses its own profile/evidence directories, and construction runs support an explicit report destination. `volt_body_review.ps1 -EvidencePath docs/evidence/volt-door-fender-fit-2026-11-03` builds the review from actual native images without additional packages.

Four Volt bases, 120 full/simple modules and the Volt Garage rest scene are rebuilt from the final source. The preceding 105 Compatibility captures are retained separately in `previous-recording`; shared Garage/build context differs from that earlier recording. A new `--body-control` capture renders the archived rejected body parts inside the current isolated showroom to provide matched lighting/camera comparisons. Plain silver/blue views and purple/red patterned liveries are reviewed under both desktop renderers. The evidence completion receipt links the accepted logs.

Initial fit checks caught a rear flank-offset applied twice and a small factory-tip height correction; those were fixed in the geometry. Construction checks then found coincident bottom rows where an extended bumper blade converged on the arch foot. The final attachment starts 3 mm above the datum and preserves a monotone section, retaining all edge-pairing and triangle tests. A full intermediate module bake was superseded and rebuilt completely. The sandbox denied attempts to stop the exact Codex-owned superseded test process trees, so the bounded runners finished normally; no owner process was targeted. Initial failures, intermediate captures and the final results are retained separately.

The evidence includes scoped before/final snapshots, source preservation checks and a binary-inclusive task-only checkpoint with forward/reverse content checks. The main Git index is untouched. No device query/test, APK, owner save/process change, real purchase, live/backend mutation or deployment was performed. Reload is required for the new module/photo revision. Owner appearance and physical-device performance acceptance remain.
